## Interpretation

`enet_a0.1_l0.5` is the better default model for H1 forecasting based on overall error (MAE 1.5373 vs 1.5461; RMSE 1.9339 vs 2.0603). The persistence baseline is stronger in fold 1, but performance degrades more sharply by fold 3, while ElasticNet remains more stable and clearly better on RMSE in later data. This suggests the linear model captures signal beyond naive carry-forward and should be preferred for alarm-budget evaluation.

